/// <p>A QVariant object holds a single value of a single <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qvariant.html#typeId" translate="no">typeId</a>() at a time. (Some types are multi-valued, for example a string list.) You can find out what type, T, the variant holds, convert it to a different type using <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qvariant.html#convert" translate="no">convert</a>(), get its value using one of the toT() functions (e.g., <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qvariant.html#toSize" translate="no">toSize</a>()), and check whether the type can be converted to a particular type using <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qvariant.html#canConvert" translate="no">canConvert</a>().</p>
