/// <p>An animation group is a container for animations (subclasses of <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qabstractanimation.html" translate="no">QAbstractAnimation</a>). A group is usually responsible for managing the <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qabstractanimation.html#State-enum" translate="no">state</a> of its animations, i.e., it decides when to start, stop, resume, and pause them. Currently, Qt provides two such groups: <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qparallelanimationgroup.html" translate="no">QParallelAnimationGroup</a> and <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qsequentialanimationgroup.html" translate="no">QSequentialAnimationGroup</a>. Look up their class descriptions for details.</p>
