/// <p>QCborStreamWriter provides a StAX-like API, similar to that of <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qxmlstreamwriter.html" translate="no">QXmlStreamWriter</a>. It is rather low-level and requires a bit of knowledge of CBOR encoding. For a simpler API, see <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qcborvalue.html" translate="no">QCborValue</a> and especially the encoding function <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qcborvalue.html#toCbor" translate="no">QCborValue::toCbor</a>().</p>
/// <p>The typical use of QCborStreamWriter is to create the object on the target <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qbytearray.html" translate="no">QByteArray</a> or <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qiodevice.html" translate="no">QIODevice</a>, then call one of the <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qcborstreamwriter.html#append" translate="no">append</a>() overloads with the desired type to be encoded. To create arrays and maps, QCborStreamWriter provides <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qcborstreamwriter.html#startArray" translate="no">startArray</a>() and <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qcborstreamwriter.html#startMap" translate="no">startMap</a>() overloads, which must be terminated by the corresponding <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qcborstreamwriter.html#endArray" translate="no">endArray</a>() and <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qcborstreamwriter.html#endMap" translate="no">endMap</a>() functions.</p>
